Greetings,

I have a need to get a cpu id in the DEC alpha unix environment, both
at the command line level, and programmatically, as I am porting an
application from AIX / HP-UX that uses this value in a licensing algorithm.

In AIX we can do a "uname -m" and in HP-UX we do "uname -i"
to return such a value. And in both environments, the uname system 
function can return the necessary value, (I think the utsname member 
name is "machine" in HP-UX).

Is there such a facility on the Alpha? The references to cpu ids that I
have found in the various include files all seem to refer to
mutli-processor
issues and not to a unique vendor-supplied id as such.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Regards,


Simon Taylor  



