Liyun Wang (Liyun.Wang.1@gsfc.nasa.gov) wrote:
: Hi,

: I am writing a Makefile in which I need to "extract" file names without
: directory paths from a target list which contains list of files with
: full directory path: e.g.

: FLIST = /usr/local/bin/file1 /usr/local/bin/file2 /usr/local/bin/file3
: ...
: $(FLIST):
: 	# Make macro AAA, from $@, which contains only file1, etc.

: How do I extract file1, file2, etc., from $@ or any of internal macros
: to form new marco AAA to be used in later part of my Makefile? I tried 

: $(FLIST):
: 	AAA=`echo $@ | sed -e "s|/usr/local/bin/||"`
: 	echo $(AAA)

: but it did not work. If any of you could help, I would greatly
: appreciate it.

Digital Unix make supports the F suffix, which applies to the filename
part of the variable. In your case it could be used as:

$(FLIST):
	echo ${@F}


Hope this is what you needed.


