Younghan Kim wrote:
> 
> I have two alpha server 2100 using Digital unix V3.2d-1.
> there are neither gated nor routed in two systems.
> Insted of dynamic routing, they routed statically.
> Two systems connected same network(192.10.249.11 and 192.10.249.12).
> The router address is 192.10.249.1
> System A(192.10.249.11) can't ping to 192.10.2.x but can telnet.
> but System A can ping to another network (192.10.4.x)
> 
> System B(192.10.249.12) can ping and can telnet.
> 
> When i tried to ping to System A(192.10.249.11) from 192.10.2.x,
> System A(192.10.249.11) Responded.


I see this ocasionally with static routes, when the connection has
been lost and then reestablished. 'telnet' and 'rsh' work fine but
ICMP type connections like ping and traceroute do not work. The
fix is easy. Do a 'route delete ....' and a 'route add ...' to
get rid of the bad route and to setup the new. 

Charlie 

