In article <33436A22.237C228A@ucc.uni-sofia.bg>, Hristo Kirov <hristo@ucc.uni-sofia.bg> writes:

>I am trying to put Micropolis 1924 disk (SCSI 2.1GB) on Alpha server 400
>runing Digital UNIX V4.0A. But disksetup says that disk capacity is 1GB.
>When I try to change disk geometry to something else newfs fails.

What does scu(8) say?  Use the "show capacity" command.

	# scu -f /dev/rrz#c show capacity

	replacing '#' for the unit number and if that doesn't
	work, use the explicit bus, target and LUN number.

What does the label say?  Use the disklabel command.

	# disklabel /dev/rrz#c

p.s.  What is "disksetup"?  The only thing close I can find on a
V4.0B system is voldisksetup.
--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




