>Hi,
>
>	In Digital UNIX 4.0, if I allocate the 'pthread_mutex' on 
>shared memory, can I use that mutex for synchronisation among the 
>threads in different processes ?

pthread_mutexs can be either PTHREAD_PROCESS_PRIVATE (default) which
means they only work between threads in the same process, or they
can be PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED in which case they work between threads
in different processes also.

I am pretty certain (but not 100%) that Digital UNIX 4.0 does support
PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED. Check man pages for pthread_mutexattr_init()
and pthread_mutexattr_setpshared() for how to set PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED.

