Kamal Kishore Mantri wrote:
> 
>         I want to intialize some global data & acquire few
> system resources(mutexes, shared memory .. etc) when shared
> library is loaded. Similiarly these resouces need to released
> when shared library is unloaded. Can anybody suggest me a way
> of doing this in Digital UNIX 4.0. In HP-UX , it could have
> been done with +I_INITIALIZER flag in ld.

Two ways:

1) Create a routine with the name __init_[anything], for example,
   __init_mylib. The loader will call all routines with this format
   when the library is loaded. Similarly, __fini_[anything] routines
   are called before the library is unloaded.
2) Use the ld options -init <name> and -fini <name> to cause specific
   functions to be called at load and unload time.

