No, Digital UNIX does not (yet) support PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED. This is
an optional POSIX feature, which for various reasons (priority,
schedule, etc.) we initially chose not to implement. I can promise that
we WILL support it in the future. (I'll even tell you that the new
X/Open brand followon to UNIX95, called UNIX98, requires the pshared
option, along with several other POSIX options.)

You can always tell whether a system supports the pshared attribute by
looking in <unistd.h> for the symbol _POSIX_THREAD_PROCESS_SHARED. If
defined, then the "pshared" attribute is supported -- if not defined,
the attribute is not supported.

