I'm afraid you're out of luck.  We run the bulk of our systems on AXPpci33
boards (at least for now), and there is _no way_ to run NT on an OSF board
or the other way around.  You see, when they designed the AXPpci33 board,
they skimped on firmware--they only used firmware big enough to hold SRM
*or* ARC.  ARC is used for NT, SRM for DU.  

You'll have to run NT on these things.  But you can get FX!32 from Digital,
which will let you run most Intel-NT binaries.

Good luck!

Jeremy Anderson
