I believe this is incorrect.  Yes, when you buy one of these boards it comes
only with the ARC (or SRM) console.  But you *can* download the "other"
firmware/BIOS and re-flash the chip.  The stipulation in the manual included
with the board I bought is that if your board has the AT-style keyboard it
can't run OSF (because OSF doesn't support that keyboard). If you have a
PS/2 style keyboard connector you can use either OS -- you just need to get
the appropriate firmware and reflash.

Maybe, though, there are different board revs and some of them can't be
altered.

I don't have the URL handy, but there's a site at Digital from which you can
download new firmware revs.  If anyone needs it, let me know and I can poke
through my address book.

